# AIDA distributed store (orphan branch worktree)
# Pattern matches both the directory (in the canonical worktree) and a
# symlink (in `aida session start`-created sibling worktrees, which
# point back at the canonical store). Without the bare-name pattern,
# git treats the symlink as a tracked file. trace:EPIC-21 | ai:claude
.aida-store/
.aida-store

# AIDA runtime state — deny-by-default. Anything under .aida/ is per-clone
# runtime state (cache, sessions, roles, env shims, review prompts, server
# data, etc.) unless explicitly allow-listed below. Adding a new runtime
# file under .aida/ requires no gitignore change; tracking a new
# project-config file requires adding an explicit `!.aida/<name>` line.
# trace:BUG-73 | ai:claude
.aida/*

# Tracked exceptions: project-level config that lives in the repo.
!.aida/config.toml
!.aida/reserved-paths.toml
!.aida/docker-compose.yml
!.aida/docker-compose.dev.yml
!.aida/setup.sh
.antigravitycli/
docs/writeups/

# SPIKE-31: per-clone derived rules generated by `aida rules sync` from
# the spec graph. Regenerated on demand; would thrash across worktrees if
# committed. Hand-authored rules outside this subdir remain tracked.
.claude/rules/aida-specs/
